"""
Internal administrative-boundary overlay (raion/"district") lines for
Kyiv Oblast and Cherkasy Oblast only -- a display-only special case, same
as ``app.data.oblast_settlements``, per the Threat Movement redesign.
No other oblast has this data; nothing here changes any other oblast's
map rendering or any non-visual behavior (Telegram, risk analysis,
movement parsing are untouched).

Source: slawomirmatuszak/ukrainian_geodata (rayony.geojson -- Ukraine's
136 post-2020-reform raions), free and open, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/):
https://github.com/slawomirmatuszak/ukrainian_geodata
Which of the 136 raions belong to Kyiv/Cherkasy Oblast was verified
empirically (each raion's centroid tested against this project's own
``region_at_point``/``REGION_RINGS``), not assumed from name alone.

Coordinates are already projected into this project's shared SVG
viewBox space with ``app.ukraine_geo.project_lat_lon`` (same projection
as ``REGION_RINGS`` and the region-border rendering already on this
map), and simplified with Douglas-Peucker (epsilon=0.6 viewBox units)
to cut point count roughly 4-5x for smooth mobile rendering while
keeping each raion's shape recognizable -- these are meant to be read as
a light internal-border overlay, not a survey-grade boundary.
"""

